# Telecom Support Triage Agent

This repository contains a professional telecom support triage API designed to classify support queries, prioritize customer issues, and route them into an operational queue.

## Overview
The project is built with FastAPI and follows a small but scalable service structure. It accepts customer support queries, detects the likely issue category, ranks urgency, prepares an automated response, and stores the ticket for agent review.

## Project structure
```text
.
├── finalproject/
│   ├── app/
│   ├── config/
│   ├── requirements.txt
│   ├── run.py
│   ├── README.md
│   └── tests/
├── README.md
├── TELECOMM LLD.pdf
├── TELECOMM Project HLD.pdf
└── Telecomm Support Triage Report.pdf
```

## Getting started
```bash
cd finalproject
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python run.py
```

The API will be available at:
- http://localhost:8000
- http://localhost:8000/docs

## Core improvements made
- Fixed config path resolution for reliable startup from any location
- Corrected ticket model and API response payloads
- Added customer name tracking and dashboard summary logic
- Added health endpoint and service status monitoring
- Improved validation for invalid input data
- Added production-friendly API metadata and route structure
- Added tests for stability and regression prevention
- Added professional documentation and repo structure

## Testing
```bash
cd finalproject
pytest -q
```
